Iron Will represents the culmination of the Iron Body discipline, where the
monk's mental fortitude becomes so powerful that it manifests as physical
protection. Through absolute mastery of mind over matter, the monk can
partially resist all forms of physical damage through sheer force of will.

This passive skill provides broad damage reduction against physical attacks.
Unlike the other Iron Body skills which harden specific body parts, Iron Will
creates a mental barrier that supplements all other defenses. The protection
applies automatically whenever the monk takes physical damage.

Achieving Iron Will requires mastery of the earlier Iron Body techniques.
Only by first conditioning the flesh, skin, bones, muscles, and legs can
a monk develop the deep understanding of their physical form necessary
to protect it through mental discipline alone.

The monk who attains Iron Will becomes extraordinarily resilient, their
body seemingly absorbing punishment that would fell lesser warriors. This
toughness, combined with the monk's other defensive abilities, makes them
surprisingly durable despite their lack of heavy armor.

